<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
Below you see graphs of the functions <m>y=-x^4</m>,   <m>y=\frac{1}{4}x^4</m>, and  <m>y=x^4</m>. Decide which is which.
</p>

<image width="50%" xml:id="ex_4_3_11">
<shortdescription>
A short description.
</shortdescription>
<latex-image label="ex_4_3_11_fig">
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\begin{axis}[grid=none,
xmin=-3,xmax=3,
ymin=-3,ymax=3,
legend pos = south east,
xtick=\empty,
ytick=\empty,
minor tick={},
xlabel={}, ylabel={},
]
\addplot[domain=-2.5:2.5] {x^2};
\addlegendentry{A}
\addplot[domain=-2.5:2.5,red] {-x^2};
\addlegendentry{B}
\addplot[domain=-2.5:2.5,orange] {0.3*x^2};
\addlegendentry{C}
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
</latex-image>
</image>


</statement>

<solution>
<p>
A is <m>y=x^4</m>; B is <m>y=-x^4</m>; C is <m>y=\frac{1}{4}^4</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
The area, <m>A</m>, of a unilateral triangle whose sides have length <m>a</m> is given by:
<md>
A=\frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}a^2.
</md>
Find the side length <m>a</m>, in cm, which gives the area <m>A</m> equal to <m>8 \text{ cm}^2</m>. Round off your answer to three decimal places.
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
<m>4.298</m> cm
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>



</exercises>